From: jetson-nixos contributors
Subject: [PATCH] host1x: allow the context bus without the in-tree driver

The external host1x driver uses host1x_context_device_bus_type, but disabling
the in-tree host1x driver also drops its selection of this hidden symbol.
Give the existing context-bus option a prompt so an external-driver kernel
can select it independently, without enabling a competing host1x driver.

Keep the bus built in: drivers/iommu/iommu.c includes it in iommu_buses only
when CONFIG_TEGRA_HOST1X_CONTEXT_BUS is enabled. Defining the missing symbol
in the external module alone would not preserve IOMMU bus notifications.

Target: Linux v6.18.46 drivers/gpu/host1x/Kconfig
Upstream-Status: Pending
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/host1x/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/host1x/Kconfig
@@ -1,7 +1,12 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 
 config TEGRA_HOST1X_CONTEXT_BUS
-	bool
+	bool "Tegra host1x context device bus"
+	depends on ARCH_TEGRA || COMPILE_TEST
+	help
+	  Build the context device bus and its IOMMU integration independently
+	  of the in-tree host1x driver. Enable this when using an external
+	  host1x driver. The in-tree driver selects this automatically.
 
 config TEGRA_HOST1X
 	tristate "NVIDIA Tegra host1x driver"
